commit 131be896d4fb99ca8cf8427a17a6208fe74a0acf
Author: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Wed Aug 19 08:45:48 2026 +0000

    Fix eyelid arc flattening and white-line flash on blink
    
    The curved eyelid boundary was computed over EYE_IMAGE_WIDTH (350px)
    while only the centered 240px are visible on screen, so the visible
    columns fell almost entirely in the flat part of the dome and the
    curve looked like a straight line. It was also faded out via
    arc_taper as the blink progressed, flattening it further right when
    it's most visible, while relying on that same taper to guarantee full
    closure at BLINK_LEVEL_MAX.
    
    Rebuild the arc dome over the new EYELID_ARC_WIDTH_PX (visible width)
    and drop arc_taper in favor of an overshoot in base_cutoff_f, so the
    curve stays constant throughout the blink while the center column
    still reaches full closure. Add an EYELID_SNAP_CLOSED_PX threshold to
    force full closure once few pixels remain open, avoiding a flash of
    sclera in the final frame before BLINK_HOLDING.

